Platform and toolchain libraries
--------------------------------

The fork's Linux release is dynamically linked on Ubuntu 24.04; the shared
libraries required by each release are listed in its DEPENDENCIES.txt. Those
library packages are supplied by the distribution under their own
GPL-3.0-compatible licenses (MIT/BSD-style, LGPL-2.1-or-later and Apache-2.0)
and are not redistributed in the release archive. The fork's release archive
ships LICENSE and this notice alongside the binaries. It does not embed musl
or the Linux libraries listed below. Optional fully static Linux builds can
embed those libraries; their listed versions describe the upstream
static-build baseline, not the fork's dynamic release.

The Windows release is a single executable built with MSYS2/MinGW, statically
linked to its GCC runtime. Toolchain versions follow the build environment,
not fixed package versions in this notice. The macOS app links Apple's system
frameworks in addition to the bundled font libraries listed above.

